WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:07.600
[Presented by....U.S. Public Health Service.
Federal Security Agency. A Sound Masters Production]

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.900
[Written by...Oscar Saul. Photography...James
Lillis. Music...Tom Bennett. 

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:18.200
Narrator...Arnold Moss. Directed by...Owen Murphy.]

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:25.700
[A marching band in uniform marches down the street in formation, led by a drum major.]

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:30.200
[Banner reading We Can Do It Again hangs from upstairs windows in a house, with people leaning out waving.]

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:40.100
[Marchers and music continue; children are shown lining the street.]

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:50.360
This is the portrait of a veteran.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:57.370
This is the portrait of a man who was ready
to do whatever his country asked.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.619
This is the portrait of a veteran who would
fight again if he could.

00:01:13.619 --> 00:01:16.210
[Elderly man walks slowly with walking canes
in both hands]

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:21.490
No, he wasn't wounded. It wasn't an enemy
shot that crippled him. It's not a wound of

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:23.640
battle that makes him walk this way.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:27.780
Yet, this soldier was crippled by the war.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:33.289
He was one of the tens of thousands of men
who were mobilized. Away from home, away from

00:01:33.289 --> 00:01:35.420
friends, away from old habits.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:41.200
He was struck by an enemy in the blood by
a germ: the spirochete.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.740
The germ that causes syphilis.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:48.710
Syphilis that came and seemed to go away, but stayed in the blood to cripple him later on.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:55.500
This is the portrait of the veteran of World
War I. A portrait of one of the thousands

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.550
of soldiers just taken from duty by syphilis.

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:04.520
One of the thousands crippled, some killed,
by the enemy in the blood.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:11.520
But, this is a sickness and death that is
preventable. Syphilis can be fought and beaten.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:15.730
And in the laboratory they are fighting it.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:20.510
In the laboratory, they found new and powerful
weapons against syphilis.

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:25.500
There's the microscope test that searches
out the spirochete and helps the doctor find

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:26.890
an early infection.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:33.090
There's the blood test that can search the
blood for syphilis. Doctors send blood samples

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:36.060
here for laboratory testing.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:42.920
[Images of three people appear in front of
the technician]

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:51.660
The technician examines the blood and finds
-- negative. This patient is not infected.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:56.420
[Image of man on the left smiles and disappears.]

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:04.070
Negative. This patient is not infected.

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:07.580
[Image of woman on the right smiles and disappears]

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:14.000
Positive -- danger. This patient may have
syphilis and the doctor examines him for other

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:17.060
signs and does a second blood test to check
the first.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:19.200
[Image of man in the middle looks distressed and disappears]

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:25.060
If the patient is infected, then it can be
treated. Infection can be fought with the

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:26.670
weapons of the laboratory.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:33.350
The infection can be conquered if the patient
takes the full course of treatment.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:39.010
The laboratory's found the chemicals that
cure syphilis: bismuth, mercury, arsenic.

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:45.760
Early treatment with these chemicals is insurance
against a child born dead or crippled. Insurance

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:48.220
against a heart weakened by syphilis.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:53.860
Yes, the battle in the laboratory is well
fought, but this is only half the fight.

00:03:53.860 --> 00:04:00.700
Here, is where the other half of the fight
is to be made. Here in the schools and colleges.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:05.720
Here where syphilis strikes at the fighting
strength of the country and the Navy.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:11.670
And among the soldiers, here, we must fight.
And in the mills and plants where the nation's

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:13.840
work is done.

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:19.880
Here, where the people are. This is where
venereal disease strikes.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:22.900
And this is where the other half of the fight
must be fought.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:28.500
It can only be fought here, among the people
and by the people. By people who know the

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:33.710
enemy, how he strikes, and how to strike back.

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:40.710
Know the danger spots of the city, the places
where the disease begins.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:45.920
[A sign in front of an establishment reads Joe's]

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:53.419
[People are seen dancing inside Joe's.]

00:04:55.990 --> 00:05:01.819
The places that infect the city and infect its
people. The places with the easy pickups.

00:05:01.819 --> 00:05:08.819
Yes, these are the danger spots...the places that breed syphilis.

00:05:12.039 --> 00:05:18.739
Know the other danger spots. The dark,
the hidden streets, the places that are whispered about.

00:05:18.739 --> 00:05:23.639
[A man walks slowly down a darkened street.]

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:28.980
These are the danger spots. Here, the disease begins. Yes, here it begins.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:30.819
[Aerial view of city]

00:05:30.819 --> 00:05:33.539
Here, a new chain of infection starts.

00:05:33.539 --> 00:05:38.339
A chain of infection that will take lives
of children to be born and bring people to

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:41.779
hospitals, to insanity, and to blindness.

00:05:41.779 --> 00:05:42.729
Here, it begins...

00:05:42.729 --> 00:05:45.769
[Image of one family with lines extending
out it.]

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:50.740
and spreads, from one part of the
city to another. From one person to many people.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:54.700
One infected person carrying infection to
many people; 

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:57.140
the infection spreading from them to countless others.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:05.920
[Four lines extend out from a image of a man labeled 'Infected," to reach four women.]

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:13.240
[Man ambles down darkened street toward a storefront with a white sign reading "Men's Doctor.]

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:16.839
And with the disease, come the quacks.

00:06:16.839 --> 00:06:21.349
The charlatans who thrive wherever people
are ignorant, who bring disaster wherever

00:06:21.349 --> 00:06:23.789
people have failed to fight syphilis.

00:06:23.789 --> 00:06:27.210
The quacks who promise cures, but never cure.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:31.960
[An ad reading Treat Syphilis with Dr. Welch's 6006 looms in front of the man.]

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:37.120
Authoritative voice: Don't worry, kid. I can cure you. It's no worse than a bad cold. I'll clear it up for ya. 

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:39.580
Here, drink this. Cure is guaranteed!

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:41.720
[Ads for remedies promising cures appear and grow larger in front of the man, whose back is turned.]

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:45.300
Quack: 30 years as a specialist in men's diseases,
a dollar a bottle, it's cheap, kid - you can't

00:06:45.309 --> 00:06:48.930
go wrong with this stuff. You can't go wrong!

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:53.550
You can't go wrong! You can't go wrong!

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:56.439
[Health Department. Veneral Disease Clinic]

00:06:56.439 --> 00:07:01.699
But he can go wrong. He will go wrong unless
the people fight with knowledge, with treatment,

00:07:01.699 --> 00:07:04.900
with blood tests to search the enemy out.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:11.900
Yes, the people must fight to guard against
the blindness that syphilis may cause.

00:07:12.669 --> 00:07:15.830
To prevent the insanity the disease can bring.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:22.379
To prevent the crippling, the broken minds,
the twisted limbs, the suffering and the poverty.

00:07:22.379 --> 00:07:24.229
All these the people must fight.

00:07:24.229 --> 00:07:29.900
And the fight must be swift and hard because
every day the casualties mount.

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:33.669
Thousands of sick and idle, and important
jobs are left undone.

00:07:33.669 --> 00:07:35.930
Production is sabotaged by syphilis.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:42.930
[Amount of raw material to be processed piles
up over time]

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:48.149
And men already under arms are struck by the
disease.

00:07:48.149 --> 00:07:54.139
In 1917, the army lost seven million days from active duty. Syphilis is the sniper, the saboteur

00:07:54.139 --> 00:07:55.860
behind the lines.

00:07:55.860 --> 00:08:01.960
But it strikes not in the field, not in the
camps, but in the towns. That is where syphilis

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:04.229
must be fought.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:11.800
So, if the people learn, they'll go to the
doctors in the clinics to find the skills

00:08:12.029 --> 00:08:13.270
that will make them safe.

00:08:13.270 --> 00:08:19.300
If each person will guard himself, he can
help destroy this waster of America.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:23.699
He can save his own and the nation's strength
for production.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:30.700
For the nation's security. For all the work
and joy of living.

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:48.660
The people can raze this shadow from the land,
from their homes, if the people learn,

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:50.950
if they fight syphilis.

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:59.900
[The End. A Sound Masters Production]

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:04.660
[U.S. Public Health Service. 1798]

